# cut — fail
#
# Failing to harvest a part from a body. The verb needs a CORPSE, and a corpse only exists after a kill — so
# unlike every other verb test this one has to make its own subject first: slay the chicken, then cut
# the carcass.
#
# Two things about that make this worth having as a test rather than trusting the verb audit:
#
#   * a spawned corpse is not observable until NarrativeController.SyncSpawnedObservations reconciles
#     it into the narration graph, which is built once from the areas as the factory left them. Before
#     that sync existed the body was in the area and the player was never told;
#   * the corpse OPENS the next observation phase by itself — PendingCorpseObservations is drained
#     ahead of everything else — so the second half of this script does not have to hunt for it.
#
# `goal` is set twice for the same reason cli/tame/success.cli sets it twice: two different verbs in
# one run, and the playground's goal draw is otherwise uniform over everything the object offers.
#
# Both halves are Required verbs now, so the knife is combined TWICE — once to make the corpse and
# once to open it. It is the reference tool of both, so neither combination reaches the item critic
# (which picks at random under --playground and would otherwise decide this test by seed).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item knife --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon --observe-only "chicken"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# ── Make the corpse ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
strategy succeed
goal slay
advance 12 180
regions

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect SUCCESS
expect-verb slay

# ── Now cut it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The corpse opens the phase on its own, so the keyword is whatever it left behind.
click button
advance 12 180
regions

# Only the CUT misses. The kill above must still succeed, or there is no corpse to fail against —
# `strategy` is a preset consulted at every roll, so it is switched here rather than at the top.
strategy fail-dice
goal cut
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect FAILURE

# What makes this a cut test rather than an any-verb test.
expect-verb cut
# The failure assertion that means something: the verb's own consequence did NOT happen.
# Asserting the wound instead would be flaky — FailurePenalties samples one slot in five,
# so most failures injure nobody.
expect-no-outcome corpse_item_acquisition
quit
